53287.sol:
The given curve is $\left(\frac{x}{a}\right)^n+\left(\frac{y}{b}\right)^n=2\begin{aligned}
& \Rightarrow n\left(\frac{x}{a}\right)^{n-1} \cdot \frac{1}{a}+n\left(\frac{y}{b}\right)^{n-1} \cdot \frac{1}{b} \frac{d y}{d x}=0 \\
& \Rightarrow \quad \cdot \quad \frac{d y}{d x}=-\frac{b}{a} \frac{\left(\frac{x}{a}\right)^{n-1}}{\left(\frac{y}{b}\right)^{n-1}}
\end{aligned}$<br/>At $(a, b), \frac{d y}{d x}=-\frac{b}{a} \frac{(1)^{n-1}}{(1)^{n-1}}=-\frac{b}{a}\therefore$ The tangent at $(a, b)$ is
$\begin{array}{cc}
\Rightarrow & y-b=-\frac{b}{a}(x$-a) \\
\Rightarrow & a y-a b=-b x+a b \\
\Rightarrow & b x+a y=2 a b \\
\Rightarrow & $\frac{x}{a}+\frac{y}{b}=2
\end{array}$

54795.sol:
Let one mole of each gas has same volume as $V$. When they are mixed, then density of mixture is
$\begin{aligned}
\rho_{\text{mixture }} & =\frac{\text{ mass of } \mathrm{O}_2+\text{ mass of } \mathrm{H}_2}{\text{ volume of } \mathrm{O}_2+\text{ volume of } \mathrm{H}_2} \\
& =\frac{32+2}{V+V}=\frac{34}{2 V}=\frac{17}{V}
\end{aligned}$
Also, $\rho_{\mathrm{H}_2}=\frac{2}{V}\begin{aligned}
\text{Now, velocity } v & =\left(\frac{\gamma P}{\rho}\right)^{1 / 2} \text{$ or $} v \propto \frac{1}{\sqrt{\rho}} \\
\frac{v_{\text{mixture }}}{v_{\mathrm{H}_2}} & =\sqrt{\left(\frac{\rho_{\mathrm{H}_2}}{\rho_{\text{mixture }}}\right)} \\
& =\sqrt{\left(\frac{2 / V}{17 / V}\right)}=\sqrt{\left(\frac{2}{17}\right)}
\end{aligned}$

